    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense enters today with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.43) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Gunnar Henderson** stands as the premier start, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Melton and the added leverage of wind blowing out, which boosts his already elite base projection. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a breakout day against the high-xERA Lorenzen; while his score is bolstered by a dynamic platoon advantage, his multi-category upside\u2014specifically the push for stolen bases\u2014makes him a cornerstone of today's optimal configuration. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also warrants attention, as he effectively weaponizes a strong matchup against Bieber, with SP skill metrics suggesting he is due for a high-efficiency outing.\n\nThe bottom half of the lineup, particularly **Jacob Wilson** (70.77) and **Kyle Tucker** (67.25), provides the depth necessary to hunt for stolen bases. **Jacob Wilson** is a dark horse today, capitalizing on an ideal lead-off spot and a favorable park factor, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a solid play despite the moderate challenge presented by Castillo. Among our bench options, **Sam Antonacci** (47.88) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly falling behind **Liam Hicks** (48.50). While **Sam Antonacci** possesses the benefit of a premium lead-off spot, the optimizer favored **Liam Hicks** for his superior platoon splits against Nola. We are flagging the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Curtis Mead**, **Andy Pages**, **Wade Meckler**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jacob Wilson** as a primary risk factor; should any of these players drop significantly in their respective batting orders, we may see a volatility spike in their daily production.",
